WEBVTT

00:00:00.010 --> 00:00:10.380
 <i>Urashima Taro</i> 
As Told By Yukariko

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.560
Hey, Hayate-kun!

00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:04.710
We've been waiting for this! Yay!

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:07.560
Once upon a time, there was

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:09.980
a young man named Urashima Taro.

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:14.110
One day, as Urashima 
strolled the beach,

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:13.400
<i>Oh! Melon bread!</i>

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:16.300
he came upon some kids
 tormenting a turtle.

00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:21.040
"Hey! Don't torment the 
turtle like that!"

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:25.920
He shouted from a spot far 
enough from them to run away.

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:29.360
"What you say?" responded the children.

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:31.630
"Shaddup, ol' man."

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:33.980
"Let's get 'im!"

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:39.490
And the turtle chimed in: 
"Yeah! Let's get him!"

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:42.490
Urashima dashed over and

00:00:42.490 --> 00:00:44.290
beat the turtle with his fishing pole.

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:47.000
"Don't repay goodness with evil!"

00:00:47.410 --> 00:00:50.350
Urashima's cries echoed
 up and down the shore.

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:51.660
And he lived happily ever after.

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:53.220
What an awful story.

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:54.930
What was the moral?

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:55.960
Right?

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:57.650
To be continued!

00:00:57.650 --> 00:00:59.040
It <i>continues</i>?

00:00:59.040 --> 00:00:59.800
Continues where?

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:00.800
And how?

00:01:08.490 --> 00:01:12.000
<i>Once upon a time, there 
was a very poor boy.</i>

00:01:12.460 --> 00:01:14.240
<i>The boy had long since lost</i>

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:15.990
<i>his parents, so he lived alone...</i>

00:01:15.990 --> 00:01:17.700
<i>...in a poor town, 
in a poor country.</i>

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:22.120
<i>The boy said: "I'm gonna 
 make it big one day!"</i>

00:01:22.120 --> 00:01:25.170
<i>He repeated this as 
he grew, until he became...</i>

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:26.560
<i>...a fine, fine robber.</i>

00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:28.590
<i>The man said: "I wanna be admired</i>

00:01:28.590 --> 00:01:30.600
<i>as the best robber 
in the business."</i>

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:33.300
<i>There's always a weird 
community somewhere.</i>

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:38.460
<i>Near the man was a woman who reigned 
supreme over the robber business.</i>

00:01:38.890 --> 00:01:41.420
<i>She said: "I bet you'd 
command great respect</i>

00:01:41.420 --> 00:01:44.470
<i>if you stole the black camellia."</i>

00:01:45.010 --> 00:01:47.230
<i>He took her at her word,</i>

00:01:47.230 --> 00:01:49.730
<i>and began a journey 
to find the black camellia.</i>

00:01:53.220 --> 00:01:56.770
<i>At last, he tracked down the 
location of the black camellia</i>

00:01:57.220 --> 00:02:00.340
<i>to a castle deep in the middle of a forest.</i>

00:02:01.790 --> 00:02:04.360
<i>The man sneaked in immediately.</i>

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:08.650
<i>However, the castle guards 
immediately fought back.</i>

00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:13.560
<i>Then, as he was running for his life,</i>

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:15.860
<i>in the depth of the castle he found...</i>

00:02:19.220 --> 00:02:24.280
<i>...the world's most beautiful princess.</i>

00:03:57.220 --> 00:04:01.590
<i>Mommy, why did you marry Daddy?</i>

00:04:02.070 --> 00:04:03.230
<i>Well,</i>

00:04:04.190 --> 00:04:06.300
<i>he was incredibly handsome!</i>

00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:09.810
<i>My youthful mind thought that 
was the worst reason ever.</i>

00:04:12.320 --> 00:04:15.240
<i>But Shin-chan was a bit careless, too.</i>

00:04:15.770 --> 00:04:17.190
<i>Careless?</i>

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:18.320
<i>Right.</i>

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:21.190
<i>For example, he lost his wedding ring.</i>

00:04:22.530 --> 00:04:24.860
<i>Oh. So, so...</i>

00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:26.790
<i>Is that expensive?</i>

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:30.910
<i>Super expensive.</i>

00:04:31.130 --> 00:04:34.050
<i>Really? How much was it? How much?</i>

00:04:47.750 --> 00:04:49.390
It's been a while...

00:04:50.330 --> 00:04:52.430
...since I dreamed about my mother.

00:04:53.770 --> 00:04:58.270
<b> Weather Report</b>

00:04:53.770 --> 00:04:58.270
<b>Typhoon #12
Atmospheric pressure
Wind speed</b>

00:04:54.110 --> 00:04:55.780
<i>Now for the weather outlook.</i>

00:04:55.780 --> 00:04:58.690
<i>A massive low pressure system is</i>

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:00.230
<i>approaching Japan from the south.</i>

00:05:00.610 --> 00:05:02.100
<i>According to the Japan 
Meteorological Agency,</i>

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:04.460
<i>an unusual tropical 
cyclone has developed...</i>

00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:03.780
Good morning.

00:05:04.380 --> 00:05:07.700
Huh? What's going on here, Miss Nagi?

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:09.680
You're up so early!

00:05:12.220 --> 00:05:13.610
<i>It is now 12:00 PM.</i>

00:05:13.610 --> 00:05:15.240
<i>It's time for the news at noon.</i>

00:05:16.230 --> 00:05:18.250
It's kinda insulting to say that

00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:19.610
noon is early for me.

00:05:19.610 --> 00:05:22.170
Then make it a habit to wake up earlier.

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:24.110
Oh, whatever.

00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:26.700
Get me an iced café au lait.

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:29.050
Sure. Please wait a moment.

00:05:29.710 --> 00:05:33.410
It's already the second half of 
Silver Week. Are you sure it's okay?

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:34.850
What's okay?

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:36.560
America.

00:05:36.920 --> 00:05:38.310
Don't you need to go...

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:41.820
...collect your deceased father's things?

00:05:43.720 --> 00:05:46.290
Does it really matter?

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:49.090
I have no interest in my father.

00:05:51.340 --> 00:05:55.290
Oh. We received photos of 
your father's belongings.

00:05:58.270 --> 00:06:00.450
Huh? What's this?

00:06:00.880 --> 00:06:02.810
Looking at these is pointless.

00:06:03.370 --> 00:06:07.220
I can't tell if it's my 
father's stuff or not.

00:06:07.690 --> 00:06:09.180
That's true.

00:06:10.440 --> 00:06:12.600
I mean, why now?

00:06:13.360 --> 00:06:15.560
That's right. Maria-san had said...

00:06:17.460 --> 00:06:21.010
<i>The officers in Las Vegas who sent us</i>

00:06:21.010 --> 00:06:23.660
<i>these photos told me something chilling.</i>

00:06:23.660 --> 00:06:26.050
<i>There's a reason why her father's</i>

00:06:26.050 --> 00:06:28.100
<i>belongings went missing for 13 years.</i>

00:06:29.760 --> 00:06:31.520
Why?

00:06:31.520 --> 00:06:35.870
All the police personnel 
and estate appraisers

00:06:35.870 --> 00:06:39.500
involved have died in 
unfortunate accidents.

00:06:44.350 --> 00:06:49.580
Therefore, the Las Vegas police 
department moved the stuff

00:06:49.580 --> 00:06:52.460
to a highly secure location 
where nobody could touch it.

00:06:52.960 --> 00:06:54.370
That's how things were left.

00:06:55.460 --> 00:06:57.490
Oh, I see.

00:06:59.300 --> 00:07:01.570
I definitely don't wanna go now.

00:07:01.570 --> 00:07:03.190
Right?

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:05.960
Let's forget about it.

00:07:05.960 --> 00:07:10.060
If I don't go, they'll get 
rid of his belongings.

00:07:10.060 --> 00:07:14.580
I'd rather spend my break 
having fun with you, Hayate!

00:07:14.890 --> 00:07:17.810
I'm sorry, I have to go shopping...

00:07:17.810 --> 00:07:20.430
Why? Why do you have to go shopping now?

00:07:20.430 --> 00:07:23.310
So we can make your dinner, Miss Nagi.

00:07:23.310 --> 00:07:25.960
Thanks. Thanks a lot, but...

00:07:25.960 --> 00:07:27.340
I'm off, then.

00:07:27.340 --> 00:07:29.010
You're really leaving?

00:07:32.980 --> 00:07:36.520
You can wait for me at 
the mansion, you know.

00:07:36.520 --> 00:07:38.940
Humph. What I do is my choice.

00:07:38.940 --> 00:07:40.540
So? What are you getting?

00:07:40.540 --> 00:07:42.560
Games? Anime Blu-rays?

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:44.560
<b> Hanamura Meats</b>

00:07:42.870 --> 00:07:44.560
I'm not buying any of that.

00:07:45.120 --> 00:07:46.910
Whoa! This is...

00:07:48.070 --> 00:07:49.820
<b><i> Fish Sausages 
115mg calcium per serving</i></b>

00:07:48.070 --> 00:07:49.820
<b><i>Includes Free God 
of Conquest Stickers!</i></b>

00:07:50.090 --> 00:07:52.230
Hayate! Get me this! This!

00:07:52.630 --> 00:07:57.090
What? Maria-san will be 
upset if we buy that.

00:07:57.090 --> 00:07:58.600
It's all right.

00:07:58.600 --> 00:08:00.790
Fish sausages are good for you.

00:08:00.790 --> 00:08:02.830
There's tons of calcium in them!

00:08:03.340 --> 00:08:07.340
Oh, all right. We'll 
get the fish sausages.

00:08:07.780 --> 00:08:08.810
Okay.

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:10.340
Excuse me.

00:08:10.720 --> 00:08:12.970
I'll take three homemade fish sausages.

00:08:13.370 --> 00:08:14.340
Thanks!

00:08:16.030 --> 00:08:17.070
You idiot!

00:08:17.070 --> 00:08:20.120
Why are you buying the 
normal fish sausages?!

00:08:21.340 --> 00:08:23.090
You said they were good for you!

00:08:23.090 --> 00:08:24.930
With tons of calcium!

00:08:24.930 --> 00:08:28.570
Yes, but those sausages 
don't come with a prize!

00:08:28.570 --> 00:08:30.150
So that's what you wanted.

00:08:31.390 --> 00:08:33.630
Whatever! You're an idiot, Hayate!

00:08:33.630 --> 00:08:35.980
I'm gonna hang out with Chiharu 
and the others in the apartment.

00:08:35.980 --> 00:08:38.470
So go buy some green peppers 
or carrots or whatever...

00:08:38.470 --> 00:08:41.380
...and make beef stroganoff or something!

00:08:45.700 --> 00:08:49.670
Okay, so I don't know the way.
Take me to the apartment!

00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:53.320
Take me!

00:08:53.320 --> 00:08:54.450
Okay, okay.

00:08:57.420 --> 00:08:59.680
I'll come pick you up later.

00:09:03.160 --> 00:09:06.190
Hey, Chiharu! Kayura!

00:09:07.530 --> 00:09:10.980
That's funny. No one's here?

00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:14.490
Sender: Chiharu Harukaze

00:09:13.310 --> 00:09:14.030
Oh.

00:09:15.410 --> 00:09:16.650
I forgot.

00:09:21.390 --> 00:09:22.950
Shoot.

00:09:27.230 --> 00:09:29.400
I have to go shopping.

00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:34.410
Man, I really screwed up.

00:09:37.780 --> 00:09:42.600
So that means no one is home.

00:09:43.650 --> 00:09:47.350
I'm not scared just 
because no one is around.

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:51.370
What? Why?

00:09:51.370 --> 00:09:53.650
Why do old houses make weird noises?

00:09:56.080 --> 00:10:01.660
I-If I stay here by myself, 
I'll die of some curse or something.

00:10:06.360 --> 00:10:07.870
Big sister?

00:10:10.320 --> 00:10:11.590
Tsugumi?

00:10:11.590 --> 00:10:14.470
What happened? 
Why were you screaming?

00:10:14.470 --> 00:10:17.990
I-I didn't scream!

00:10:19.210 --> 00:10:20.940
Are you by yourself?

00:10:20.940 --> 00:10:24.310
Yes. Even Nishizawa had something to do.

00:10:24.310 --> 00:10:26.310
Now, why are you... Oh!

00:10:26.310 --> 00:10:28.810
Did you come to see me?

00:10:29.210 --> 00:10:32.560
No, no. Why would I come see you?

00:10:32.560 --> 00:10:34.840
Why do you say stuff like that?

00:10:34.840 --> 00:10:36.830
I'm your cute little sister!

00:10:35.580 --> 00:10:38.110
<i>I've never thought of 
you as my little sister!</i>

00:10:38.720 --> 00:10:41.620
If you're the only one 
here, I'm going home.

00:10:42.310 --> 00:10:44.330
W-Wait!

00:10:55.140 --> 00:10:58.440
Look at that rain, big sister!

00:10:58.440 --> 00:11:01.970
I don't think you should go home.

00:11:02.870 --> 00:11:04.310
Oh, okay.

00:11:04.310 --> 00:11:08.480
You can tell me about yourself 
until the rain stops.

00:11:09.280 --> 00:11:10.150
Huh?

00:11:12.340 --> 00:11:14.980
<b>Connecting</b>

00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:14.980
<b>Theater</b>

00:11:13.790 --> 00:11:14.980
<b>Part A</b>

00:11:15.220 --> 00:11:18.420
We're going on a trip during
 Silver Week in order

00:11:18.420 --> 00:11:20.470
to uncover an ancient mystery.

00:11:20.470 --> 00:11:21.490
Ancient mystery?

00:11:21.490 --> 00:11:23.740
<i>To America</i>

00:11:21.490 --> 00:11:23.740
<i>Easter Island</i>

00:11:21.490 --> 00:11:23.740
<i>Territory of Chile</i>

00:11:21.490 --> 00:11:23.740
<i>Pacific Ocean</i>

00:11:21.490 --> 00:11:23.740
<i>South America</i>

00:11:21.490 --> 00:11:23.740
<i>Chile</i>

00:11:21.880 --> 00:11:23.740
We're going to Easter Island in

00:11:23.740 --> 00:11:25.900
America to look at Stonehenge.

00:11:25.900 --> 00:11:27.600
What? Don't you...

00:11:27.600 --> 00:11:29.590
I'm going to interject here.

00:11:29.590 --> 00:11:31.370
Don't you mean the Moai statues?

00:11:31.370 --> 00:11:34.060
What are you talking about, Hayata-kun?

00:11:34.060 --> 00:11:36.780
The Moai statues are in Shibuya!

00:11:36.780 --> 00:11:38.010
What?

00:11:38.900 --> 00:11:41.760
<b>Connecting</b>

00:11:39.490 --> 00:11:41.760
<b>Theater</b>

00:11:40.320 --> 00:11:41.760
<b>Part B</b>

00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:47.260
How can we go see Ruka's 
concert in Las Vegas for free?

00:11:47.750 --> 00:11:51.770
I've no idea. Except maybe 
take an airplane.

00:11:52.130 --> 00:11:54.770
Nagi-chan, you always solve 
everything with money.

00:11:55.160 --> 00:11:58.730
But there are things money can't solve.

00:11:58.730 --> 00:12:01.150
It sure solves your problems.

00:12:02.510 --> 00:12:04.540
<i>The robber had just met the</i>

00:12:04.540 --> 00:12:07.670
<i>world's most beautiful princess 
inside the castle.</i>

00:12:07.670 --> 00:12:10.600
<i>After a moment of admiration, he said:</i>

00:12:11.440 --> 00:12:14.830
<i>"I know! I'll take this beautiful 
princess as my hostage,</i>

00:12:14.830 --> 00:12:17.380
<i>grab the black camellia, and escape."</i>

00:12:17.750 --> 00:12:19.080
<i>"Hey, little girl!</i>

00:12:19.080 --> 00:12:22.510
<i>Keep quiet if you don't wanna get hurt!"</i>

00:12:23.550 --> 00:12:26.600
<i>But the robber quieted after seeing</i>

00:12:26.600 --> 00:12:28.510
<i>the princess' .44 Magnum.</i>

00:12:29.160 --> 00:12:30.890
<i>God is cruel.</i>

00:12:30.890 --> 00:12:31.770
<i>Huh?</i>

00:12:32.290 --> 00:12:35.160
<i>I don't have very long to live.</i>

00:12:35.160 --> 00:12:35.870
<i>Oh.</i>

00:12:35.870 --> 00:12:37.400
<i>But I do want to fall in love.</i>

00:12:37.850 --> 00:12:40.670
<i>So I've been hoping to meet</i>

00:12:40.670 --> 00:12:44.600
<i>the man of my dreams before I die.</i>

00:12:44.600 --> 00:12:46.780
<i>But it's taking so 
long for him to appear!</i>

00:12:47.670 --> 00:12:53.370
<i>So I've been praying to the stars: 
"Do something about this already!"</i>

00:12:53.910 --> 00:12:56.130
<i>And here you are.</i>

00:12:57.480 --> 00:13:00.880
<i>You're not the kind of man I was imagining...</i>

00:13:01.370 --> 00:13:05.110
<i>...but I doubt the man of 
my dreams is coming, so...</i>

00:13:08.290 --> 00:13:11.020
<i>...you can be that man.</i>

00:13:13.090 --> 00:13:18.400
<i>But we don't know anything 
about each other, so...</i>

00:13:20.700 --> 00:13:23.530
<i>...you need to become my butler.</i>

00:13:24.070 --> 00:13:26.280
<i>Why should I become your butler?</i>

00:13:27.590 --> 00:13:29.970
<i>I will! I will be your butler!</i>

00:13:31.190 --> 00:13:33.600
<i>And that's how the two met.</i>

00:13:40.560 --> 00:13:42.670
Hey, Tsugumi...

00:13:43.290 --> 00:13:45.420
Tell me what your agenda is.

00:13:45.880 --> 00:13:47.930
M-My agenda?

00:13:47.930 --> 00:13:50.180
Your reason for getting close to me.

00:13:50.670 --> 00:13:52.660
I-I don't have one!

00:13:52.660 --> 00:13:54.120
It's out of love, big sister! Love!

00:13:54.120 --> 00:14:00.930
You can cut that out already. 
I know you're not a bad guy.

00:14:01.620 --> 00:14:05.190
If you're honest with me,

00:14:05.190 --> 00:14:07.490
maybe I can help you fulfill your wish.

00:14:07.930 --> 00:14:08.700
Really?

00:14:09.190 --> 00:14:11.330
Go on. Tell me, okay?

00:14:12.330 --> 00:14:16.290
N-No! You're not tricking me.

00:14:16.290 --> 00:14:18.580
<i>You're easy enough to fool, you idiot.</i>

00:14:19.310 --> 00:14:21.840
Humph. Okay, whatever.

00:14:24.940 --> 00:14:26.460
What's that?

00:14:26.460 --> 00:14:29.550
This? It's a fish...

00:14:31.550 --> 00:14:34.460
It's foie gras, one of the 
world's top three delicacies.

00:14:34.460 --> 00:14:35.730
I've heard about it!

00:14:35.730 --> 00:14:37.590
One of those things rich people eat, right?

00:14:37.590 --> 00:14:40.030
So that's foie gras.

00:14:40.030 --> 00:14:41.620
It's too bad.

00:14:42.200 --> 00:14:44.720
If you'd just honestly told me,

00:14:44.720 --> 00:14:46.900
your big sister would have

00:14:46.900 --> 00:14:50.090
given you the rest of the foie gras.

00:14:50.090 --> 00:14:51.030
What?

00:14:54.430 --> 00:14:57.800
So delicious. It's so delicious.

00:15:07.610 --> 00:15:10.510
Foie gras is so delicious. 
 I'll just eat it all!

00:15:14.320 --> 00:15:16.380
Maybe I'll have another.

00:15:16.380 --> 00:15:17.700
What?

00:15:17.700 --> 00:15:19.940
It's really delicious.

00:15:24.410 --> 00:15:26.720
I feel bad for you, little sister.

00:15:26.720 --> 00:15:28.450
B-Black camellia.

00:15:28.450 --> 00:15:29.150
Huh?

00:15:29.460 --> 00:15:31.660
I might... be looking for...

00:15:31.660 --> 00:15:36.110
...the Sanzenin household's treasure...

00:15:36.720 --> 00:15:37.790
...the black camellia.

00:15:45.620 --> 00:15:50.420
Oh... I-I just meant I had a dream 
about something like that...

00:15:50.420 --> 00:15:53.970
I-I don't have any proof that 
something like that exists...

00:15:52.930 --> 00:15:53.970
<i>Just eat it!</i>

00:15:56.400 --> 00:15:59.130
Does the black camellia really exist?

00:15:59.130 --> 00:16:00.730
I've never heard about it.

00:16:00.960 --> 00:16:02.910
Shurly you haff!

00:16:02.910 --> 00:16:04.490
Eat first, then talk!

00:16:05.270 --> 00:16:07.830
The bwack camewia weally existsh.

00:16:07.830 --> 00:16:09.490
Okay. Wait.

00:16:10.510 --> 00:16:11.700
<b><i>Old Geezer</i></b>

00:16:13.450 --> 00:16:15.270
Hey, old geezer.

00:16:15.270 --> 00:16:17.750
Do you know about our 
family's treasure,

00:16:17.750 --> 00:16:18.700
the black camellia?

00:16:19.800 --> 00:16:22.640
It was stolen 13 years 
ago, and it's been

00:16:22.640 --> 00:16:23.710
missing ever since.

00:16:24.220 --> 00:16:25.420
So there you have it.

00:16:26.970 --> 00:16:30.370
Why? Why wasn't it 
carefully preserved?

00:16:30.370 --> 00:16:32.660
And all the rooms are a mess!

00:16:32.660 --> 00:16:36.350
Of course I couldn't find it! Argh!

00:16:36.780 --> 00:16:39.020
There's nothing I can do about it!

00:16:39.020 --> 00:16:40.850
Oh, hello?

00:16:40.850 --> 00:16:44.300
Do we have any idea who stole our treasure?

00:16:44.300 --> 00:16:47.110
I have nothing to tell 
my stupid granddaughter.

00:16:51.820 --> 00:16:54.280
Whaaa, shoot!

00:16:54.280 --> 00:16:56.670
I broke my smart phone again!

00:16:56.670 --> 00:16:59.540
I just bought it at the end of last month!

00:16:59.540 --> 00:17:00.350
What will I do?

00:17:00.350 --> 00:17:01.710
Don't ask me!

00:17:01.710 --> 00:17:05.040
This is exactly why you could 
lose a family treasure so easily!

00:17:05.040 --> 00:17:06.600
What did you say?

00:17:06.600 --> 00:17:08.790
Big sister, you...!

00:17:26.250 --> 00:17:27.230
<i>Watch Out For Sexual Molesters</i>

00:17:27.580 --> 00:17:30.820
The rain is getting bad.

00:17:31.900 --> 00:17:33.650
Are we gonna be all right?

00:17:34.210 --> 00:17:37.350
Don't you think we should 
close the storm windows?

00:17:37.350 --> 00:17:39.710
I don't know how.

00:17:40.260 --> 00:17:41.470
Big sister!

00:17:41.470 --> 00:17:42.120
Huh?

00:17:44.760 --> 00:17:45.960
The roof is leaking!

00:17:45.960 --> 00:17:47.500
Wh-Wh-Wh-What should we do?

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:49.500
Don't ask me "wh-wh-wh-what" to do!

00:17:50.400 --> 00:17:54.130
We have no choice but to call Hayate.

00:17:54.520 --> 00:17:56.880
Huh? My smart phone is gone!

00:17:56.880 --> 00:17:59.710
Of course it is! 
You just broke it, remember?

00:18:04.860 --> 00:18:06.430
We're doomed!

00:18:06.430 --> 00:18:10.110
Oh, for crying out loud.
I'll handle this!

00:18:20.570 --> 00:18:22.120
I'll help!

00:18:22.120 --> 00:18:23.530
Don't worry about it.

00:18:23.530 --> 00:18:26.430
Go check that spot where 
the roof was leaking.

00:18:26.430 --> 00:18:27.700
And all the other rooms.

00:18:27.700 --> 00:18:29.890
If they flood, we'll have big trouble.

00:18:29.890 --> 00:18:31.450
O-Okay!

00:18:48.520 --> 00:18:49.400
Big sister!

00:19:03.980 --> 00:19:05.910
Are you all right, Tsugumi?

00:19:07.320 --> 00:19:08.410
Tsugumi.

00:19:10.510 --> 00:19:14.520
I'm totally fine. But you 
need to stop spacing out!

00:19:14.520 --> 00:19:15.770
Be careful.

00:19:15.770 --> 00:19:17.280
Sorry.

00:19:17.280 --> 00:19:19.170
Let's take care of the leaks. Quick!

00:19:19.170 --> 00:19:23.160
Everyone's precious doujinshi is here.

00:19:23.910 --> 00:19:25.340
R-Right...

00:19:26.170 --> 00:19:28.070
Be strong, big sister!

00:19:28.070 --> 00:19:31.040
Yeah! Hang in there, Tsugumi!

00:20:00.830 --> 00:20:02.760
A-Are you all right?

00:20:03.080 --> 00:20:05.320
About as all right as we look.

00:20:05.320 --> 00:20:08.770
I was worried because your 
cell phone wasn't working.

00:20:09.210 --> 00:20:11.350
It was a close one.

00:20:11.760 --> 00:20:13.770
I'm glad you're okay.

00:20:20.630 --> 00:20:22.370
Hey, Tsugumi.

00:20:22.370 --> 00:20:26.290
What? I'm really tired.

00:20:26.290 --> 00:20:28.160
Why did you save me?

00:20:28.160 --> 00:20:28.990
What?

00:20:29.820 --> 00:20:32.300
We don't have the 
black camellia anymore.

00:20:32.300 --> 00:20:34.630
So there's no reason to 
pretend you're my sister,

00:20:34.630 --> 00:20:37.540
or to try to make me like you anymore.

00:20:38.890 --> 00:20:41.580
D-Does it matter?

00:20:41.580 --> 00:20:44.530
I don't need a reason to help someone.

00:20:44.530 --> 00:20:48.070
Seriously, it's hard to have 
such a troublesome big sister!

00:20:48.970 --> 00:20:50.010
Oh, I see.

00:20:51.250 --> 00:20:53.190
Yes, this is Ayasaki.

00:20:53.610 --> 00:20:56.190
It's me. Let me talk to Nagi.

00:20:56.780 --> 00:20:58.070
Grandfather?

00:21:01.890 --> 00:21:03.200
What is it?

00:21:04.280 --> 00:21:06.540
To add to our earlier discussion...

00:21:07.550 --> 00:21:11.000
The family's treasure, the black camellia...

00:21:11.970 --> 00:21:13.560
The man who betrayed Yukariko

00:21:13.560 --> 00:21:16.550
and stole it 13 years ago...

00:21:18.510 --> 00:21:22.130
It was your father, Shin Hayek.

00:22:55.400 --> 00:22:58.150
"Do you think you've won, Urashima?"

00:22:58.150 --> 00:23:00.940
Urashima answered: 
"Wh-Who goes there?"

00:23:00.940 --> 00:23:03.190
"The turtle you just defeated was

00:23:03.190 --> 00:23:06.200
the weakest of the 
Four Heavenly Turtle Kings.

00:23:06.200 --> 00:23:09.920
What a disgrace that he lost to you."

00:23:09.920 --> 00:23:11.640
The turtles had him 
surrounded, three on one!

00:23:11.640 --> 00:23:14.030
Careful, Urashima! 
Urashima's in danger!

00:23:14.030 --> 00:23:15.280
Suddenly, a loud

00:23:15.280 --> 00:23:17.900
voice came from the ocean.

00:23:17.600 --> 00:23:25.110
<b>Rooooaaaaar</b>

00:23:17.900 --> 00:23:19.430
"Sir Urashima!

00:23:19.430 --> 00:23:22.010
I, Otohime, am coming to help you!"

00:23:22.010 --> 00:23:23.340
Said Otohime as she

00:23:23.340 --> 00:23:25.190
scrambled across rough 
waters to save Urashima.

00:23:25.730 --> 00:23:30.020
Upon seeing her, 
everyone ran for their lives.

00:23:30.440 --> 00:23:33.530
I'd like to say "they lived 
happily ever after,"

00:23:34.050 --> 00:23:35.000
but it's to be continued!

00:23:35.000 --> 00:23:35.700
Oh.

00:23:35.700 --> 00:23:37.460
I saw that coming.

00:23:37.460 --> 00:23:38.520
Yeah.
